{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01TVneZQy7uBQxNDVeyGxRyw","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All done. Here's what was implemented for task #5142:\n\n**R2.1 (buffering):** `fillBlock` pre-fills a `[]byte` buffer with repeated copies of the output line up to 8192 bytes. The main loop writes this block in bulk, avoiding per-line syscalls.\n\n**R2.2 (flush before exit):** With block writes, each `Write()` sends the full block to the OS — there's no userspace buffer to flush. This satisfies R2.2 trivially.\n\n**R3.1 (exit 0 on SIGPIPE):** `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` catches the signal for a clean exit. The `isEPIPE` check in the write loop is a belt-and-suspenders fallback.\n\n**R3.2 (exit 1 on non-EPIPE errors):** The write loop calls `os.Exit(1)` for any error that isn't EPIPE.\n\n**Tests:** Added `TestExitCodeOnSIGPIPE` that verifies exit code 0 when stdout is closed early. All 7 existing differential tests continue to pass."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":28146,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"efd60324-6f55-4840-bac7-09d47bdedc87","uuid":"4f1e22b5-a08f-4af2-a9bd-5903e1533968"}
